From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] board: qualcomm: iceland: BlissROM from the menu with ABL's
 ramdisk

The menu's BlissROM entry stored the reboot reason "recovery" so that
ABL would start the Android kernel in recovery_b. The Pad 4's ABL does
not do that: it starts recovery_b only when the image there has no
kernel, and then with boot_b's kernel, which is U-Boot. An image with a
kernel in recovery_b makes ABL stop in its fastboot.

ABL does not need to start Android itself, though. U-Boot sits in
boot_b as an Android boot image (header v4, no ramdisk), so on every
start ABL already prepares the rest of an Android boot for it: the
slot's vendor_boot + init_boot ramdisks with its bootconfig block, the
DT from vendor_boot + dtbo with the Android /chosen bootargs, and the
verified-boot state. U-Boot keeps the address of that DT (x0).

- mach-snapdragon: qcom_android_chain <interface> <partition>: load the
  kernel of the Android boot image in <partition> (v3 / v4, an arm64
  Image of at most 128 MiB) to ${kernel_addr_r} and booti it with
  ABL's ramdisk (left in place) and ABL's DT, its bootargs unchanged.
  It refuses, with nothing loaded, unless ABL's DT is valid, in RAM and
  has Android bootargs, the ramdisk range is in RAM with a cpio or
  compressed start and a bootconfig trailer, the partition is unique
  and the kernel area overlaps neither. Reads storage only.
- qcom_recovery_gate [interface [partition]]: the partition can be
  named (default recovery_b, as before). The AVB footer rule stays for
  recovery_b only: ABL never starts another partition.
- env: the entry is "BlissROM=qcom_android_chain scsi boot_a", offered
  when "qcom_recovery_gate scsi boot_a" is open (fedora next to
  userdata, userdata not the Fedora disk, an arm64 kernel in boot_a,
  the unused slot-a boot partition). If the chain refuses, the menu
  returns and the boot goes on to Fedora; no reset.

Android sees a normal start of slot b: ABL's mode, slot suffix, root of
trust and bootconfig, only the kernel comes from boot_a.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig         |   4 +
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Makefile        |   2 +-
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/android_chain.c | 250 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/boot_menu.c     |  35 ++--
 board/qualcomm/iceland.env               |   4 +-
 5 files changed, 276 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/android_chain.c

